<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells 2,235 tonnes of zinc.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells 2,235 tonnes of zinc.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Defense National Logistics Agency said it sold 4,929,000 lbs, or 2,235 tonnes, of zinc for a total of $2,612,382.</p>
<p>The buyers were Hochschild Partners, I. Schumann and Co, Trademet Inc, Ingot Metal Co, U.S. Zinc, Tally Metal Sales Inc, American Alloys and Parks Pioneer Metals.</p>
<p>The next offer of zinc is scheduled for Feb 18.</p>
<p>((New York Commodities 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
